  "id": "speech-reception-threshold",
  "term": "speech-reception threshold",
  "definition": "Speech-reception threshold is a measure of how well a person can understand speech, especially when speech and background noise are presented from different locations. A lower speech-reception threshold means better speech intelligibility under those listening conditions.",
