      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s core characterization—“a measure of how well a person can understand speech”—is not explicitly stated in the provided packet text. The packet discusses SRT being measured using the German matrix sentence test, but it does not define SRT in terms of ‘how well a person can understand speech.’",
        "While the packet supports the context of separating speech and noise in space (two loudspeakers at different angles; S0N0 separation), the first sentence combines this with an unsupported, general meaning of the metric.",
        "The packet does support that “lowest (best) SRT” corresponds to improved speech intelligibility, matching the definition’s last sentence about lower SRT meaning better intelligibility under those conditions. However, this alone is insufficient because the definition’s main first claim is unsupported."
